d freeze, or a power supply (PSU) problem.'; cr_d_6008='The previous shutdown was unexpected. Possibly a power loss or the reset/power button.'; cr_d_thermal='The system shut down due to critical temperature. Check CPU and GPU cooling (fans, thermal paste, dust).'; cr_d_tdr='The graphics driver stopped responding and was reset (TDR). Possibly an overclock, undervolt or driver problem.'; cr_d_gpudrv='The graphics driver ({0}) logged an error. Update or clean-install the driver; undo any overclock.'; cr_d_ea='EA component error/termination log: {0}. EA Anti-Cheat may be closing the game silently (no Windows error report is created).'; cr_d_wmi='Windows Reliability Monitor record: {0}'; cr_none_events='No crash records in the event log for this period. If a game closes instantly without any error, Windows may not have had time to log it; then a stability test is needed rather than log searching. First step: disable XMP/EXPO in BIOS and try again; if it continues, test memory and CPU with TestMem5, MemTest86 or OCCT.'; cr_f_dump='Dump'; cr_f_bsod='Blue screen dump'; cr_f_wer='WER report'; cr_f_ealog='EA log'; cr_f_riot='Riot log'; cr_f_ac='Anti-Cheat'; cr_f_game='Game log'; cr_f_log='Log'; cr_l_crashdumps='Windows crash dump'; cr_l_minidump='Blue screen dump'; cr_l_tempdump='Temporary dump'; cr_l_wer='Windows error report'; cr_l_werq='Windows error report (queue)'; cr_l_ea='EA / Battlefield log'; cr_l_eaapp='EA app log'; cr_l_riot='Riot / Vanguard log'; cr_l_riot2='Riot log'; cr_l_be='BattlEye log'; cr_l_eac='EasyAntiCheat log'; cr_l_mygames='Game log (My Games)'; cr_l_templog='Temporary log'; cr_bb_r_log='blue screen event logging off'; cr_bb_basic='Basic recording is on (WER service, blue screen dump and event logging). App .dmp collection is off, which is the Windows default. If you turn it on, future app crashes will produce a small .dmp file.'
